@startuml
title SD Host Controller - Command Inhibit Timing Diagrams

scale 1.5

== Figure 2-11 : Timing of Command Inhibit (DAT) and Command Inhibit (CMD) with Data Transfer ==

concise "CMD line" as CMD1
concise "DAT line" as DAT1
binary "D00" as D00_1
binary "D01" as D01_1

@0
CMD1 is "Command"
DAT1 is " "
D00_1 is high
D01_1 is high

@100
CMD1 is "Response"
DAT1 is " "

@200
CMD1 is " "
DAT1 is "Write or Read\nData"

@350
DAT1 is "Last Block\nData"

@400
D01_1 is low

@450
DAT1 is " "
D00_1 is low

== Figure 2-12 : Timing of Command Inhibit (DAT) for the Case of Response with Busy ==

concise "CMD line" as CMD2
concise "DAT[0]" as DAT0_2
binary "D00" as D00_2
binary "D01" as D01_2

@500
CMD2 is "Command"
DAT0_2 is " "
D00_2 is high
D01_2 is high

@600
CMD2 is "Response"
DAT0_2 is " "

@700
CMD2 is " "
DAT0_2 is "Busy"

@850
DAT0_2 is " "
D00_2 is low
D01_2 is low

== Figure 2-13 : Timing of Command Inhibit (CMD) for the Case of No Response Command ==

concise "CMD line" as CMD3
binary "D00" as D00_3

@900
CMD3 is "Command"
D00_3 is high

@1050
CMD3 is " "
D00_3 is low

note bottom of D00_3
  The Host Controller clears D00
  if the command is issued successfully.
end note

@enduml